{"id": "28eaf902-4b72-470f-a531-f94c36796de2", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T15:09:40.869527", "source": "user", "parent_id": "6ac5ffa3-f0c9-4b33-a6a4-38dfe4dcf459", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Design-only task, so no experiment needs to be run — I just need a solid, executable plan. Before we draft the full design, do three things:\\n\\n1) Inspect the workspace/documents (track.md) and report what's actually available: the RepoBench Python split details, the exact \\\"cross_file_first\\\" setting definition, any official harness/eval scripts, and the compute/environment constraints you'll plan around (no GPU, no network, system Python). Confirm design-only scope.\\n\\n2) Propose your experiment approach at a high level: which GPT-2 variant you'd use (e.g., gpt2 vs gpt2-large vs gpt2-xl) and why, how you'd instantiate CodeLlama-7b, how cross-file context is constructed and windowed (which files precede the target, token budget, ordering), how a sample is prompted, what decoding/config you'd fix (temperature, top-p, max new tokens, beam vs sampling), and which metric you'd report (e.g., Pass@1/Pass@k, syntax-validity/execution-based pass rates) with a precise definition.\\n\\n3) Surface the consequential assumptions and uncertainties you'd have to lock in — e.g., a RepoBench version/revision for reproducibility, how \\\"pass @k\\\" is estimated with which sample counts and seeds, a fixed sample size / subsetting rule given time limits, how to handle the models' differing tokenizers/VLAs, and any known confound (e.g., GPT-2's small context vs the amount of cross-file context CodeLlama can take). Explicitly mark each choice as an assumption, not a confirmed fact.\\n\\nDon't produce the full final deliverable yet — I want the input inventory, the proposed approach, and the assumptions/uncertainties first. I'll review those before approving the main design work.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How does the performance of a small language model (e.g., GPT-2) compare to a larger code-specialized model (e.g., CodeLlama-7b) on the RepoBench Python dataset for the 'cross_file_first' setting?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
